.TH FPCLASSIFY 3 "2026-02-06" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
fpclassify, isfinite, isinf, isnan, isnormal, signbit \- floating-point classification macros
.SH LIBRARY
Math Library (libm, \-lm)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <math.h>
.PP
.BI "int fpclassify(" x );
.BI "int isfinite(" x );
.BI "int isinf(" x );
.BI "int isnan(" x );
.BI "int isnormal(" x );
.BI "int signbit(" x );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
These macros classify IEEE 754 floating-point numbers. They work with 
.BR float ,
.BR double ,
and
.B long double
arguments.
.PP
.BR fpclassify ()
returns one of the following constants:
.RS
.TP
.B FP_NAN
The argument is Not-a-Number.
.TP
.B FP_INFINITE
The argument is positive or negative infinity.
.TP
.B FP_ZERO
The argument is positive or negative zero.
.TP
.B FP_SUBNORMAL
The argument is a subnormal (denormalized) number.
.TP
.B FP_NORMAL
The argument is a normal floating-point number.
.RE
.PP
.BR isfinite ()
returns nonzero if
.I x
is finite (not infinity or NaN).
.PP
.BR isinf ()
returns nonzero if
.I x
is positive or negative infinity.
.PP
.BR isnan ()
returns nonzero if
.I x
is a NaN.
.PP
.BR isnormal ()
returns nonzero if
.I x
is a normal number (not zero, subnormal, infinity, or NaN).
.PP
.BR signbit ()
returns nonzero if the sign bit of
.I x
is set (negative).
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR fpclassify ()
returns one of the FP_* constants.
All other macros return nonzero for true, zero for false.
.SH STANDARDS
C99, POSIX.1-2001.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fabs (3),
.BR isnan (3),
.BR math (7)
